From d3df56658ca166c11fde00b05cd6f84eb58366b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:28:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] pro1xkbd: F(x)tec Pro1X keyboard matrix behind an AW9523B

A console keyboard (kbd, behind kbdmux) and an evdev device. The scan
follows the Pro1X port's Linux driver: one column driven low at a time
with the others pre-charged, two agreeing scans, ghost suppression,
polling while a key is held. INT is taken as a falling edge, the scan
runs in a task.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
